    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMIU_External/job/Laredo-TX/Instructional-Assistant-Professor-of-Chemistry_R-098161-2": {
      "title": "Instructional Assistant Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nJob Title Instructional Assistant Professor of Chemistry Agency Texas A&M International University Department Dept, Biology & Chemistry Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of the Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for an  Instructional Assistant Professor of Chemistry to begin  Fall 2027 .  TAMIU is a Hispanic Serving Institution with over 8,000 students located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The university advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement and public service, and with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit  https://www.tamiu.edu . This is a non-tenure track Instructional Assistant Professor (9-month position). This is a renewable position contingent on funding and job performance. Primary duties will include teaching introductory and upper level courses for the chemistry program. Duties also include service to the department, college and university as needed. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.  The Department of Biology and Chemistry offers BA, BS and MS degrees in Biology and a BS in Chemistry. We currently serve ~850 undergraduate majors and ~30 graduate (Masters) students. Required Qualifications The successful candidate must hold a Ph.D. Degree in Chemistry, or a related discipline. ABDs will be considered but must have degree conferred before appointment start date. We strongly encourage candidates with prior teaching experience.  We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the university. Application Process   The completed employment application must include: Letter of interest or cover letter that addresses qualifications Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts specifying conferred/ABD degree Names and contact information of three current professional references A statement of their teaching interests, experience, and philosophy. Applications must be submitted online at  https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/. For more information, contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Kameron Jorgensen, at kameron.jorgensen@tamiu.edu or 956-326-2568. INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files.   Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMIU_External/job/Laredo-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Mathematics_R-098159-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Mathematics Agency Texas A&M International University Department Dept, Mathematics And Physics Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of the Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for an  Assistant Professor of Mathematics to begin  Fall 2027 .    TAMIU is a Hispanic Serving Institution with over 8,000 students located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The university advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement and public service, and with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit  https://www.tamiu.edu/   This is a  tenure-track 9-month full-time faculty position. Primary duties will include teaching Mathematics to both undergraduate and graduate students. Other duties include maintaining an active research agenda, publishing scholarly manuscripts, and conducting research, including securing grants. Duties also include serving on department, college and university committees, as well as mentoring students. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.    The Department of Mathematics and Physics offers BA, BS and MS degrees in Mathematics and BA with a major in Mathematics with grades 7-12 certification degree programs including a fully online certificate program that emphasizes applied data analysis, statistical modeling, and ethical communication.   Required Qualifications   The successful candidate must hold a doctorate in Mathematics or Applied Mathematics. ABDs will also be considered but must have earned a doctorate before appointment. We strongly encourage candidates with Applied and Computational Mathematics coursework. We strongly encourage candidates with (a) a strong record of or potential for sustained publication in peer-reviewed journals, (b) have the potential for or prior experience with seeking and/or securing external grant funding, (c) have a strong desire to work with first generation students, and (d) have the ability to teach in areas that complement or strengthen our undergraduate and graduate courses.    We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the university.   Application Process     The completed employment application must include: Letter of interest or cover letter that addresses qualifications Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts specifying conferred/ABD degree Names and contact information of three current professional references Applications must be submitted online at  https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/.   INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files.   Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
