    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMIU_External/job/Laredo-TX/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Developmental-Psychology_R-098032-1": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Developmental Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Developmental Psychology Agency Texas A&M International University Department Dept, Psychology & Communication Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of the Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for an  Assistant or Associate Professor of Developmental Psychology to begin  Fall 2027 .    TAMIU is a Hispanic Serving Institution with over 8,000 students located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The university advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement and public service, and with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit  https://www.tamiu.edu/   This is a 9-month tenure-track or tenured Assistant or Associate Professor position in Developmental Psychology. A reduced teaching load may support research development. Primary duties will include establishing an independent, preferably externally funded, research program in Developmental Psychology that leads to publications in peer-reviewed academic journals; applying for external grants (research, infrastructure, training, and programmatic, etc.); contributing to psychology programs; and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students on research and projects. Duties also include teaching both undergraduate- and graduate-level psychology courses as needed; supporting recruitment, curriculum development, accreditation, and departmental service; and collaborating with partners on interdisciplinary research and projects. Duties also include serving on departmental, college, university, professional, and community committees. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular on-campus attendance schedule. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.    The department is multidisciplinary as it includes degrees in psychology and communication. Psychology faculty are highly productive researchers and have unique research labs to support their work. Our community and department offer extensive opportunities for bilingual and multicultural research.   Required Qualifications   The successful candidate must hold a earned doctorate in Developmental Psychology or a related field. ABD candidates will be considered but must have earned the doctorate before appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Candidates for the Associate Professor rank must hold a record of research, teaching, and service that meets TAMIU's standards for that rank. Appointment with tenure is contingent on approval by the Texas A&M University System Board of Regents. We strongly encourage candidates with a record of, or potential for, peer-reviewed publications and external funding and the ability to strengthen our psychology programs. We prefer research expertise in bilingual/multilingual, cognitive, language, or social-emotional developmental.  We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the university.   Application Process     The completed employment application must include: Letter of interest or cover letter that addresses qualifications Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts specifying conferred/ABD degree Names and contact information of three current professional references Statement of teaching experience and philosophy Statement of research interests, experience, and future plans. Applications must be submitted online at  https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/.   INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files.   Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMIU_External/job/Laredo-TX/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Curriculum---Instruction_R-098013-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Curriculum & Instruction",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Curriculum & Instruction Agency Texas A&M International University Department Educational Programs Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of the Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for an  Assistant/Associate Professor of Curriculum & Instruction to begin  Fall 2027 .  TAMIU is a Hispanic Serving Institution with over 8,000 students located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The university advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement and public service, and with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit  https://www.tamiu.edu/   This is a 9-month faculty appointment as a tenure-track assistant professor or a tenured associate professor. Primary duties will include teaching, mentoring, and advising undergraduate and graduate students/candidates in the Undergraduate Teacher Preparation Program and the Graduate Curriculum & Instruction Program. Conduct scholarly research and publish in peer-reviewed journals. Duties also include providing service to the department, College, University, community, and profession. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.    The mission of the College of Education is to prepare highly effective, culturally competent educational professionals who are equipped to understand and assume leadership positions in a global society.   Required Qualifications   The successful candidate must hold a earned doctorate in Curriculum and Instruction (C&I) or a related field. ABDs considered if degree is completed before employment. Minimum three years of EC–12 teaching experience or equivalent, 18 graduate credit hours in C&I, and current teaching certification or eligibility. Expertise in school- and community-based field experiences required. Associate Professor candidates must meet qualifications for rank and tenure, and must demonstrate substantial publications, an active research agenda, successful teaching, and faculty leadership. We strongly encourage candidates with experience in curriculum alignment, mapping, development, program evaluation, assessment, and online course development and teaching. Demonstrated scholarly record or research potential in teacher preparation, curriculum, or pedagogy relevant to national, state, and local educational contexts. We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the university.   Application Process     The first review of applications will be  11/4/2026 . The completed employment application must include: Letter of interest or cover letter that addresses qualifications Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts specifying conferred/ABD degree Names and contact information of three current professional references Applications must be submitted online at  https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/.   INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files.   Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMIU_External/job/Laredo-TX/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Special-Education_R-097921": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Special Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Special Education Agency Texas A&M International University Department Educational Programs Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of the Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for an   Assistant/Associate Professor of Special Education to begin  Fall 2027 .    TAMIU is a Hispanic Serving Institution with over 8,000 students located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The university advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement and public service, and with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit  https://www.tamiu.edu/   This is a 9-month faculty appointment as a tenure-track assistant professor or a tenured associate professor. Primary duties will include teaching across modalities, including face-to-face and online undergraduate courses and online graduate courses. Duties also include mentoring students and serving on departmental, college, university, and professional committees. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.    The mission of the College of Education is to prepare highly effective, culturally competent educational professionals who are equipped to understand and assume leadership positions in a global society.   Required Qualifications   The successful candidate must hold a doctorate in Special Education or related field required. ABDs considered for Assistant Professor if degree is completed before appointment. Associate Professor candidates must meet qualifications for rank and tenure. All specializations welcome. Current PreK–12 special education certification or eligibility required, along with PreK–12 special education classroom experience. Demonstrated teaching effectiveness or potential in face-to-face undergraduate and online graduate courses. We strongly encourage candidates with documented record of special education work in public schools; ability to teach in areas that complement and strengthen our current programs; and educational Diagnostician Certification.    We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the university.   Application Process     The first review of applications will be  11/4/2026 . The completed employment application must include: Letter of interest or cover letter that addresses qualifications Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts specifying conferred/ABD degree Names and contact information of three current professional references Applications must be submitted online at  https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/.   INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files.   Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
