    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMIU_External/job/Laredo-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Petroleum-Engineering--Drilling-Engineering-_R-097669-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Petroleum Engineering (Drilling Engineering)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Petroleum Engineering (Drilling Engineering) Agency Texas A&M International University Department School Of Engineering Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of The Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for the position of Assistant Professor of Petroleum Engineering (Drilling Engineering) to begin Fall 2027 .   TAMIU is a Hispanic-Serving Institution with over 8,000 students, located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The University advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement, and public service, with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit https://www.tamiu.edu/.   This is a tenure-track, nine-month Assistant Professor of Petroleum Engineering position. A reduced teaching load supports research development. Primary duties will include establishing an independent, externally funded research program in drilling engineering; contributing to the BS in Petroleum Engineering with primary responsibility for teaching drilling engineering courses and associated laboratories; and mentoring student research and senior design projects. Duties also include teaching other Petroleum Engineering and engineering courses as needed; supporting recruitment, accreditation, and School service; and collaborating with academic, industry, and government partners. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.   The School of Engineering offers ABET-accredited programs in Systems, Computer, and Petroleum Engineering. Its BS in Computer Science and MS in Systems Engineering launched in 2026, and its BS in Civil Engineering launches in 2027. This position will expand Petroleum Engineering faculty capacity to meet significant enrollment growth. This position is part of a strategic faculty expansion in the School of Engineering to hire 10 permanent faculty members, eight tenure-track and two instructional, beginning Fall 2027.   Required Qualifications   The successful candidate must hold a Ph.D. in Petroleum Engineering or a closely related discipline by the appointment start date. Applicants nearing completion may be considered if the degree is awarded before appointment. Candidates must demonstrate expertise in drilling engineering through research, scholarship, professional experience, or a combination thereof; be able to teach drilling engineering courses and associated laboratories, including the use of drilling simulation equipment; mentor student research; and establish an independent research program in this area. Candidates must demonstrate strength in one or more drilling areas: fluids and cementing; well planning, design, and control; managed-pressure or underbalanced drilling; well integrity and lost-circulation control; drilling optimization; or drilling and well construction for geothermal, carbon capture, utilization, and storage (CCUS), hydrogen storage, or other emerging subsurface-energy applications. Experience or demonstrated ability to pursue external research funding is especially desirable. Experience or ability to develop industry and government partnerships is also desirable.   We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the University. Application Process The completed employment application must include:  A letter of interest or cover letter that addresses the candidate’s qualifications for the position. Current curriculum vitae. Unofficial transcripts documenting the conferred degree or progress toward completion of the required doctorate. Names and contact information of three current professional references. Statement of research interests, experience, and future plans. Statement of teaching experience and philosophy.   Applications must be submitted online at https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/. Review of applications will begin on October 31, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMIU_External/job/Laredo-TX/Instructional-Assistant-Professor-of-Systems-Engineering_R-097643": {
      "title": "Instructional Assistant Professor of Systems Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nJob Title Instructional Assistant Professor of Systems Engineering Agency Texas A&M International University Department School Of Engineering Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of The Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for the position of Instructional Assistant Professor of Systems Engineering to begin Fall 2027.   TAMIU is a Hispanic-Serving Institution with over 8,000 students, located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The University advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement, and public service, with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit https://www.tamiu.edu/.   This is a fixed-term, non-tenure-track, nine-month Instructional Assistant Professor of Systems Engineering position. Initial appointments may be made for up to three years and renewed contingent upon satisfactory performance and institutional need. Primary duties will include contributing to the BS and MS in Systems Engineering by teaching courses across areas relevant to both programs. Potential teaching areas include operations research, systems simulation, facility layout and logistics, computer-integrated manufacturing, systems engineering management, engineering computational tools, advanced multivariate statistics, and advanced modeling and simulation. Instruction will emphasize project-based and hands-on learning. The successful candidate will also contribute to Senior Design projects as assigned. Duties also include teaching general engineering and other courses as needed by the School; mentoring students; and supporting experiential learning, curriculum development, ABET assessment and continuous improvement, recruitment, and School service. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.   The School of Engineering offers ABET-accredited programs in Systems, Computer, and Petroleum Engineering. Its BS in Computer Science and MS in Systems Engineering launched in 2026, and its BS in Civil Engineering launches in 2027. This position is part of a strategic faculty expansion in the School of Engineering to hire 10 permanent faculty members, eight tenure-track and two instructional, beginning Fall 2027.   Required Qualifications   The successful candidate must hold a Ph.D. in Systems Engineering, Industrial Engineering, Engineering Management, or a related discipline by the appointment start date. Applicants nearing completion may be considered if the degree is awarded before appointment. Candidates must demonstrate preparation to teach Systems Engineering courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels and the ability to develop and deliver applied, project-based, and hands-on engineering instruction. Experience or ability to mentor Senior Design or other applied student projects, use computational or simulation tools in instruction, contribute to ABET assessment and continuous improvement, or support curriculum development is highly desirable.   We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the University.   Application Process   The completed employment application must include: A letter of interest or cover letter that addresses the candidate’s qualifications for the position. Current curriculum vitae. Unofficial graduate transcripts documenting the conferred degree or progress toward completion of the required doctorate. Names and contact information of three current professional references. Statement of teaching experience and philosophy, including approaches to project-based and hands-on engineering education.   Applications must be submitted online at https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/. Review of applications will begin on October 31, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMIU_External/job/Laredo-TX/Instructional-Assistant-Professor-of-Geology_R-097640-2": {
      "title": "Instructional Assistant Professor of Geology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nJob Title Instructional Assistant Professor of Geology Agency Texas A&M International University Department School Of Engineering Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of The Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for the position of Instructional Assistant Professor of Geology to begin Fall 2027 .   TAMIU is a Hispanic-Serving Institution with over 8,000 students, located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The University advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement, and public service, with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit https://www.tamiu.edu/. This is a fixed-term, non-tenure-track, nine-month Instructional Assistant Professor of Geology position. Initial appointments may be made for up to three years and renewed contingent upon satisfactory performance and institutional need. Primary duties will include teaching geology and earth science lecture and laboratory courses, including courses that fulfill University core curriculum needs; contributing to instruction in Civil Engineering, including Hydraulics and Hydrology; and providing GIS-related instruction in Systems Engineering. The successful candidate will also support teaching in the School’s other programs as needed. Duties also include advising and mentoring students; supporting curriculum development, assessment, recruitment, accreditation, and instructional laboratory activities; and participating in School service. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.   The School of Engineering offers ABET-accredited programs in Systems, Computer, and Petroleum Engineering. Its BS in Computer Science and MS in Systems Engineering launched in 2026, and its BS in Civil Engineering launches in 2027. This position is part of a strategic faculty expansion in the School of Engineering to hire 10 permanent faculty members, eight tenure-track and two instructional, beginning Fall 2027.   Required Qualifications   The successful candidate must hold a Ph.D. in Geology, Geosciences, Earth Science, or a closely related discipline by the appointment start date. Applicants nearing completion may be considered if the degree is awarded before appointment. Candidates must demonstrate appropriate academic preparation to teach geology and earth science lecture and laboratory courses. Academic preparation or teaching experience in hydrology, water resources, environmental geology, GIS, remote sensing, geospatial analysis, or related areas supporting engineering curricula is especially desirable. Experience in laboratory or field-based instruction, curriculum development, student mentoring, or interdisciplinary teaching is also desirable.   We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the University.   Application Process The completed employment application must include:  A letter of interest or cover letter that addresses the candidate’s qualifications for the position. Current curriculum vitae. Unofficial transcripts documenting the conferred degree or progress toward completion of the required doctorate. Names and contact information of three current professional references. Statement of teaching experience and philosophy.   Applications must be submitted online at https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/. Review of applications will begin on October 31, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
