    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMIU_External/job/Laredo-TX/Spring-Adjunct-Faculty--Communications---On-Campus-_R-097391-1": {
      "title": "Spring Adjunct Faculty (Communications) (On Campus)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nPart time\n\nJob Title Spring Adjunct Faculty (Communications) (On Campus) Agency Texas A&M International University Department Dept, Psychology & Communication Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Social Sciences seeks to establish a pool of qualified applicants for future, part-time Fall Adjunct Faculty appointments in Sociology. Successful applicants may teach up to six (6) semester credit hours within the required discipline as dictated by student demand, hold office hours, and assist students as needed. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus.    Education and Experience: ·         Master’s degree in the discipline, or a closely related area with a minimum of 18 graduate hours in Communication.   Preferred Qualifications: ·         An earned doctorate in the discipline (or closely related field) with a minimum of 18 graduate hours. ·         Previous teaching experience at the collegiate level. ·         Prior relevant industry experience.   Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: ·         Ability to communicate effectively, orally and in writing.  ·         Ability to interact effectively and professionally with the general public.  ·         Ability to plan, organize, and prioritize tasks.  ·         Ability to work under stress and with pressing timelines.  ·         Ability to maintain confidentiality.   Other information: ·         The above job duties may not be performed in every Adjunct Faculty position and might not include all related duties that may be performed. ·         Adjunct Faculty positions are temporary appointments, assigned per semester and on an as-needed basis. ·         These temporary appointments are for the Spring 2027 semester and/or any applicable Spring 2027 Sub-terms.   Application Procedure: During the application process you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and Submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience \" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Completed employment applications must include: ·         Curriculum Vitae ·         Letter of Interest addressing qualifications ·         At least 3 current professional references and their full contact information, and ·         Unofficial transcripts   Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered.  Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application.  “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application.  Incomplete applications will not be considered.   All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMIU_External/job/Laredo-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Criminal-Justice_R-097352-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice Agency Texas A&M International University Department Dept, Social Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of the Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for an Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice to begin  Fall 2027 .  TAMIU is a Hispanic Serving Institution with over 8,000 students located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The university advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement and public service, and with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit  https://www.tamiu.edu/ This is a full-time tenure-track position. Primary duties will include teaching undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral courses; conducting research; and mentoring students. Duties also include serving on departmental, college, university, and professional committees as well as mentoring students. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.  The Program in Criminal Justice is housed within the Department of Social Sciences, which is within the College of Arts & Sciences. For more information, please visit our website at https://www.tamiu.edu/coas/dss/index.shtml . Required Qualifications The successful candidate must hold  a PhD in Criminal Justice or a related field. Candidates who are ABD will also be considered but must have earned their degree before August 16, 2027. All specializations will be considered but preference will be given to those with expertise in border security, homeland security, security studies, GIS, immigration, or a related area. We strongly encourage candidates with strong research skills, strong records of or potential for sustained publication in peer-reviewed journals, and the potential for or prior experience with seeking and/or securing external grant funding.  We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the university. Application Process   The completed employment application must include: Letter of interest or cover letter that addresses qualifications Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts specifying conferred/ABD degree Names and contact information of three current professional references Applications must be submitted online at https://www.tamiu.edu/adminis/ohr/employment/ . For more information, contact the search committee chair, Dr. Eileen Huey, at ehuey@tamiu.edu . INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMIU_External/job/Laredo-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Communication-Sciences-and-Disorders_R-097135-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Communication Sciences and Disorders",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Communication Sciences and Disorders Agency Texas A&M International University Department College Of Nursing & Health Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Laredo, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M International University (TAMIU), a member of the Texas A&M University System, welcomes applicants for an  Assistant Professor of Communication Sciences and Disorders to begin  Fall 2027 . TAMIU is a Hispanic Serving Institution with over 8,000 students located in Laredo, Texas, a vibrant and bicultural city with a population of about 250,000. The university advances knowledge through research and discovery, teaching and learning, community engagement and public service, and with an intentional focus on student success and research excellence. For more information, please visit  https://www.tamiu.edu/ This is a 9-month tenure-track position. Primary duties will include teaching assigned courses in Communication Sciences and Disorders program; evaluating students’ progress in coursework; completing the administrative aspects of assigned courses; supervising field-based students or student internship when needed; demonstrating scholarly productivity through publications in referred journals and attendance at professional conferences and meetings; and assisting in the development of a Master's program. Duties also include providing service to the department, college and university. This position requires face-to-face interactions through a regular schedule of attendance on campus and in the workplace.  The College of Nursing and Health Sciences prepares skilled professionals who promote health, wellness, and quality of life. The College values excellence in teaching, scholarship, service, and community engagement. Required Qualifications The successful candidate must hold a doctorate in Communication Sciences and Disorders or related field from a regionally accredited institution. ABDs will also be considered but must have earned a doctorate before appointment. Candidates must demonstrate potential for teaching, peer-reviewed scholarship, external funding, and supporting first-generation students, and hold or be eligible for Texas SLP licensure and/or ASHA CCC-SLP certification. We offer competitive salaries and a benefits package including health insurance, retirement benefits, and life insurance. Additional pay is available for summer teaching. Financial support for professional development opportunities, such as attending academic conferences, is also provided. Moving expenses are covered in whole or in part by the university. Application Process   The completed employment application must include: Letter of interest or cover letter that addresses qualifications Current curriculum vitae Unofficial transcripts specifying conferred/ABD degree Names and contact information of three current professional references Applications must be submitted online at  https://www.tamiu.edu/admins/ohr/employment/ . INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process, you have only one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and submit the application. You will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once you “Submit” the application materials. The software does not allow you to “Save” your application and return to complete the process at a later time. The page \"My Experience\" has an area provided under Resume/CV to drop or upload files. Applications received by Texas A&M International University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
